+### Design
+49d-1. Record layout in `depth_spill_frame.rs` (magic `TVDF`, version 1, kind, payload length ≤ `FRAMED_MAX_PAYLOAD` = one replay POST body, rows, `capture_seq` range, payload CRC-32, header CRC-32). `append_v1_records` splits the payload on line boundaries (`ilp_chunk_ranges`), builds every header before it takes `DEPTH_SPILL_APPEND`, then under the lock opens, `fstat`s, writes and on failure cuts back to the end of the last record it wrote in full; it never syncs. `spill_failed_depth_ilp` writes the framed file when `DEPTH_SPILL_WRITES_FRAMED` (true), syncs the payload on the synced paths, then `sync_dir_entries` syncs the file's entry and the spill directory's entry when this process has not synced them yet (tracked in `AppendState` under the same lock, at most 64 entries, cleared when full; a replay removal voids a mark in flight). Spill writes stay where they were (writer thread, rescue thread, parked rescue, the drain's inline fallback through `off_worker`); nothing new runs on the drain. `replay_framed_spill_dir` runs after the text pass in the depth directory round: snapshot the length under the lock, stream from the resume offset through one `REPLAY_STREAM_BUFFER_BYTES` window (`FramedCursor`), filter each kind-1 `market_depth` record on the arrival clock and POST it; a permanent refusal isolates lines; a record refused whole is set aside as `.refused-records`, three in a row quarantine the file; corrupt bytes, a torn tail, kind 2 and other tables are set aside byte for byte; at the end the file is removed under the lock only if it did not grow.
+### Edge Cases
+49d-1: a crash mid-append (torn tail at every cut offset); a failed write with a failed cut-back (fragment resynced and set aside); bit rot in a header or payload (CRC refuses, resync to the next whole record); a false magic inside a payload; a record larger than the window (asserted impossible, tiny-window test still advances); an append landing while the replay drains (beyond the snapshot, kept for the next round); two appenders at once (lock, no interleave); the drain's unsynced inline fallback creating the hour file and a synced append following it; the replay removing a file between an append and its directory sync; the spill directory created by this write; a one-row poison batch first in an hour followed by good batches; every record refused (table-level); a line longer than one record (refused before any byte); legacy `.ilp` files in the same folder; kind-2 bytes holding `\n` and spaces; a multi-record batch whose write fails in its second record (the first stays and replays); a table-level refusal that starts after an earlier record was accepted (refused line for line, still quarantines on the third); the newest legacy depth `.ilp` after the switch (emptied, not held as live).
+### Failure Modes
+49d-1: a failed file sync or directory sync is an `Err`, so the caller marks the range unapplied and counts it as today, and the next synced append retries the directory sync; a failed set-aside or POST stops the round and resumes at the record boundary; a refused record is kept in quarantine and counted on `tv_tick_spill_replay_lines_rejected_total{dir="depth"}` (the `market-data-refused` loss group, no new counter in it); a whole-file quarantine keeps every byte; a crash leaves at most a torn tail, set aside and counted. Honest limits (also in the CLAUDE.md row): the drain's inline fallback can wait for another appender's open, `fstat` and write; only the innermost level `create_dir_all` makes is directory-synced; a false magic with a valid header CRC (about 2^-32) at a window edge can set real bytes aside (kept); the CRC cost is Assumed (~20 ms per 8 MiB) until the `#[ignore]`d harness is run on the prod box.
+### Test Plan
+49d-1: `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 cargo test -p tickvault-storage --lib` (filters `depth_spill_frame`, `depth_spill_framed_replay`, `depth_persistence`, `tick_spill_replay`), `--test spill_rescue_sync_guard`, `--test session_window_gate_guard`, the depth DHAT tests (`crates/*/tests/dhat_*depth*`), the common guards (`claude_md_codebase_map_guard`, `error_code_rule_file_crossref`, `error_code_tag_guard`, `assertion_free_test_ratchet`), clippy `-D warnings` on storage and app, `cargo fmt --check`, and a bite check on each review fix (the old `created = start == 0` rule, the CRC under the lock, the first refused record quarantining the file, the corrupt span counted as 1).
+### Rollback
+49d-1: set `DEPTH_SPILL_WRITES_FRAMED = false` and the writer goes back to the text `.ilp` file byte for byte; the framed replay keeps draining any `.ilpf` already on disk, so no file is stranded. Reverting the whole PR before any `.ilpf` exists is clean; after one exists, keep the reader (revert the writer only) or move the files aside, since the old text pass never reads `.ilpf`. No table, schema, alarm or infrastructure change.
+### Observability
+49d-1: every set-aside is a coded `TICK-SPILL-01` `error!` with a `source` (`depth_framed_corrupt`, `depth_framed_torn_tail`, `depth_framed_unsupported`, `depth_framed_wrong_table`, `depth_framed_record_refused`, `depth_framed_lines_rejected`, `depth_framed_file_quarantined`, `depth_framed_accepted_not_removed`); a deferred round is a coded `warn!` (`depth_framed_replay_deferred`); a failed cut-back is `HOT-PATH-02` `depth_framed_cut_back_failed`. Counters: `tv_depth_spill_frame_set_aside_bytes_total{reason}` (diagnostic, seeded at 0 for every reason, outside the loss groups) and the existing `tv_tick_spill_replay_lines_rejected_total{dir}` for rows. Runbook: `docs/error-runbooks/tick-spill-replay-error-codes.md` §5.
